    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "An egoless programming team approach holds everyone equally responsible, treats the process as separate from the individuals, and focuses on correcting faults rather than placing blame on any particular developer. The egoless team structure is democratic, and all team members vote on a decision, whether it concerns design considerations or testing techniques. When a fault is discovered or a failure occurs, the egoless development team is concerned with correcting the fault, not with placing blame on a particular developer.",
