[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "The textbook argues that high-level Petri nets are better suited because they avoid the limitations of strictly sequential state-machine models when multiple preliminary events must occur before treatment can begin. It notes that a state-machine could either specify only a single order of events or become overly complex by enumerating all possible sequences, whereas Petri nets—and by extension high-level Petri nets with their extensions—handle concurrent and data-dependent control more naturally, modeling the pre-transition activities without forced sequencing or explosion of states.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "A state-machine model of the emergency room might specify only a single order of events, thereby excluding several acceptable behaviors, or it might specify all possible sequences of events, resulting in an overly complex model for a relatively simple problem. A Petri net model of the same emergency room nicely avoids both of these problems.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ],
    "type": null
  }
]

[
  {
    "role": "paragraph",
    "segment": "A delay in an activity on the critical path pushes all subsequent critical path activities forward, forcing them to be late, too, if there is no slack. The longest path has a slack of zero for each of its nodes, because it is the path that determines whether or not the project is on schedule. For this reason, it is called the critical path.",
    "citations": [
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "Notice what happens when an activity on the critical path begins late (i.e., later than its earliest start time). The late start pushes all subsequent critical path activities forward, forcing them to be late, too, if there is no slack.",
        "img_id": null
      },
      {
        "type": "source_text",
        "content": "The longest path has a slack of zero for each of its nodes, because it is the path that determines whether or not the project is on schedule. For this reason, it is called the critical path.",
        "img_id": null
      }
    ]
  }
]

